{%- comment -%}
  Inline SVG library.

    {% render 'svg-icons', icon: 'value-props-icon-true-bounce', class: 'value-props__icon' %}

  Params
    icon   required. One of the `when` values below.
    class  optional. Applied to the <svg> element.

  COLOUR
    The four value-prop icons are drawn in `currentColor`, so they take the
    CSS `color` of whatever contains them — one property, inherited, and
    hover/focus states on the parent work without extra rules. They shipped
    filled with the accent; the mockup renders them near-white, which is why
    the fill is no longer baked in.

    The two logo lockups are white paths plus an accent chevron. The chevron
    fill is `var(--brand-accent)` rather than currentColor — currentColor
    would flatten it into the wordmark. The accent hex itself lives only in
    assets/tokens.css (`--bronze`); nothing here hardcodes it.

  SIZING
    No width/height attributes — size these from CSS. Each icon keeps its
    viewBox so it scales cleanly.

    Most are square (24x24), but not all — `usap-approved` is a 118x72
    lockup. Size from `height` with `width: auto` at the call site rather
    than pinning both to the same value, or the wide ones letterbox inside a
    square box and render at a fraction of their legible size.

  NOTE: the case variable was `svg-icons`, which Liquid cannot resolve —
  hyphens are not legal in variable names, so it evaluated to nil and no
  `when` branch ever matched. Renamed to `icon` and passed as a parameter.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- case icon -%}

